WATER-WALKING EXERCISE — ADVANCED CHAKRA CONTROL
Konohagakure Genin / Chunin Training

Purpose: To refine the constant, precise chakra control begun in the
tree-walking exercise. Standing and moving on water demands continuous
adjustment rather than a fixed output.

Method:
1. Emit chakra from the soles of the feet to form a repelling surface on
   the water.
2. Unlike solid bark, water requires a steady, dynamically-balanced flow;
   the amount must be adjusted moment to moment to stay afloat.
3. Practice standing, then walking, then sparring while maintaining the
   technique.

Notes: This skill underlies many water-nature techniques and mobile
combat over rivers and lakes. Trainees typically master tree-walking
first. Falling in is expected — train at a safe depth with a spotter.
When water-walking becomes second nature, chakra control is sufficient
for most field ninjutsu. Supervised by Jonin sensei.
